<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patwardhan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Patwardhan family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Patwardhan were a Chitpavan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> family from the Konkan whose members rose as cavalry commanders under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwas</a> in the 18th century. Rewarded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jagir">jagirs</a> in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> country, they fought in the wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>. Their holdings became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Sangli, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miraj">Miraj</a>, Jamkhandi and Kurundwad, which joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948.</p></div>
